From f42aebc800793a24f48f72a5c54b03429a2acb22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Kenan=20Kasumovi=C4=87?=
 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:56:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(sdlgpu): give each vertex program its own shader

ub_vs interprets the vertex program per vertex, keeping temporaries,
inputs and outputs in arrays it indexes at run time. Adreno keeps those
in memory: on a Retroid Pocket 6 the menus ran at 6-10 fps at 1280x720
with the GPU at 100%.

Each program now gets ub_vs compiled with VSPEC around a straight-line
vs_prog (nv2a_vspec.c, every field a constant and every register its
own variable), by SDL_shadercross on a worker thread. The build embeds
ub_vs preprocessed with VSPEC as text for it. Draws use ub_vs until the
variant is ready. RECOMP_VS_SPEC=0 turns it off, =sync compiles on the
drawing thread, and RECOMP_SHADER_CACHE keeps the SPIR-V between runs.
---
